@notes-done-toggle
Feature: Notes Done-Toggle (Web App)
  As a user managing personal notes
  I want to tick a note as done or not done directly from the notes list
  So that I can flip a note's completion status without leaving the list and see the saved state after a reload

  Background:
    Given I am signed in to the web app
    And the notes list is displayed with at least one note

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the core in-list toggle: ticking a note marks it done and visually distinguishes it
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A done note is visually distinguished by a struck-through or dimmed title
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The done state is represented as a boolean done flag (done: true / done: false) rather than a completed field or a status enum
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Ticking a note in the list marks it as done
    Given a note in the notes list that is not done
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the note should be marked as done
    And the note's title should be visually distinguished as done

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the reverse direction: unticking returns the note to the not-done state
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Unticking a done note in the list returns it to not done
    Given a note in the notes list that is done
    When I untick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the note should be marked as not done
    And the note's title should no longer be visually distinguished as done

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 constraint — the control is operable directly from the list without opening a note detail view
  @key-example
  Scenario: The completion control is operable without opening the note detail view
    Given a note in the notes list that is not done
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the note should be marked as done
    And I should not have opened the note's detail view

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — the tick is saved through the existing PATCH /api/notes/{id} endpoint carrying the done flag
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The tick control updates optimistically while the PATCH is in flight and reconciles to the server-confirmed state on response
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Ticking a note saves the done state through PATCH /api/notes/{id}
    Given a note in the notes list that is not done
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the web app should send PATCH /api/notes/{id} carrying the done flag set to true
    And the displayed state should match the server-confirmed done flag

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — the untick is saved through the same endpoint carrying the done flag set to false
  @key-example
  Scenario: Unticking a note saves the not-done state through PATCH /api/notes/{id}
    Given a note in the notes list that is done
    When I untick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the web app should send PATCH /api/notes/{id} carrying the done flag set to false
    And the displayed state should match the server-confirmed done flag

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — a failed save must never leave the list showing a completion state that was not saved
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A failed save is indicated by an inline failure message on the affected note row
  @negative
  Scenario: A failed save reverts the tick control and shows a failure indication
    Given a note in the notes list that is not done
    And the save request for the note will fail
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the note's completion control should revert to not done
    And I should be shown a failure indication

  # Why: FEAT-PO-003 — the saved done state is read back from the backend after a reload, not held only in client memory
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The notes list read path (GET of notes) returns the done flag for each note so the control can render its persisted state on load and after reload
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A note ticked as done appears ticked after a reload
    Given a note in the notes list that has been ticked as done and saved
    When I reload the notes list
    Then the note's completion control should appear ticked
    And the ticked state should come from the backend's stored note data

  # Why: FEAT-PO-003 — the saved not-done state is likewise read back from the backend after a reload
  @key-example
  Scenario: A note returned to not done appears unticked after a reload
    Given a note in the notes list that has been unticked to not done and saved
    When I reload the notes list
    Then the note's completion control should appear unticked
    And the unticked state should come from the backend's stored note data

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 / ASM-004 — the done state is binary, so the control accepts only the two states and no intermediate status
  @boundary
  Scenario Outline: The completion control accepts only the two binary states
    Given a note in the notes list in the <initial> state
    When I set the note's completion control to <target>
    Then the note should be in the <target> state
    And no intermediate completion status should be recorded

    Examples:
      | initial   | target    |
      | not done  | done      |
      | done      | not done  |

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — re-applying the same flag is idempotent and answers the same note (settled by the contract: "Setting the flag to what it already is answers the same note")
  @boundary
  Scenario: Re-applying the same done flag answers the same note
    Given a note in the notes list that is already done
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list again
    Then the note should remain done
    And the displayed state should match the server-confirmed done flag

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — a note that does not exist (or belongs to another user) answers one indistinguishable not-found, so the list cannot display a saved state for it
  @negative
  Scenario: Saving a note that does not exist answers one indistinguishable not-found
    Given a note in the notes list whose save request answers not-found
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the save should be refused with a not-found answer
    And the note's completion control should revert to its previous state

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — the PATCH body carries the done flag alone, so the note's label and creation time stay the row's own and come back unchanged (settled by the contract)
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The PATCH /api/notes/{id} body carries the done flag alone and the endpoint accepts it
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Saving the done flag leaves the note's other fields untouched
    Given a note in the notes list with a label and a creation time
    When I tick the note's completion control in the list
    Then the note's label should remain unchanged
    And the note's creation time should remain unchanged

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — the write surface is reachable only by a signed-in owner; an unauthenticated save is challenged rather than applied
  @negative
  Scenario: An unauthenticated save is challenged rather than applied
    Given I am not signed in to the web app
    When the web app attempts to save a note's done state through PATCH /api/notes/{id}
    Then the save should be refused with a sign-in challenge
    And the note's completion state should remain unchanged
